#HELPS



0 mailing 'mailing list'~
In order to facilitate setting up games, we have set up a mailing
list to find times that work for people.

To request an invite to the mailing list, either send an email
to pkmud@pkmud.net, or go to the following URL:

https://groups.google.com/forum/?fromgroups=#!forum/pkmud

In addition, we have connected the game to Twitter.  Player logins
are broadcast on the @PKmudAnnounce account.
~

0 high 'high score'~
Syntax: high

This command gives a listing of the highest rated players in
the game.
~

0 snare~
Syntax: snare

The snare skill allows your character to tie a snare at his present
location which will trip the next character that walks into the room.

This tripped person will be disoriented briefly, and will find their
butt sitting on the ground.
~

0 CVIEW~
Syntax:  cview
Syntax:  cview <class>

Cview without an argument gives a list of classes, whether they are
enabled or disabled, and their ratings relative to other classes, based
on when more experienced players play them.

Cview with a class shows a list of skills, stats, and abilities which
a class has.
~

0 RATING~
The rating system is based on the difference in character's ratings.

It changes when a player kills a player, you get a doom, or are
linkdead at the end of the war.

Doom = rating goes down 30 points.
Linkdead at the end = rating goes down 15 points.

For kills, the change is calculated as follows:
If the killer is 400 points higher than the victim,
there is no change.

Otherwise, the change is:
30 * ( 1 / ( 1 + 10 ^ ( difference / 400 ) ) )

This is similar to the ladder ranking systems used in professional chess,
tennis, and in the Starcraft ladders.
~

0 FOLLOW~
Syntax: follow <the leader>

This will allow you to follow the person you follow.  There are,
however, restrictions.

Players that are out of war can only follow out of war characters.

Otherwise, you can only follow players when you succeed at the
follow skill, which is checked in every room.
~

0 STATISTICS CONSTITUTION STRENGTH DEXTERITY WISDOM INTELLIGENCE~

Constitution affects how much damage you take.  You take one less
point of damage per point of constitution above 16.

Dexterity affects your armor class.  Your armor class is reduced by
10 for every point of dex above 14, until 18 dex, then approximately
3 for every point beyond that.  It also affects how many items you
can carry.

Intelligence affects the level of a cast spell.  For every point of
intelligence beyond 16, your casting level is increased by 1.
Your spellcasting level is reduced by one for every point of intelligence
below 11.

Strength affects your hit and damage rolls, how heavy a weapon you
can wield, and how much weight you can carry.

Wisdom currently doesn't do anything.
~

0 SPAM SPAMMER SPAMMING~
Spam is a general term for repeating something over and over and
over and over and over and over and over and ...

It's derived from the Monty Python Spam skit, where a couple
(both guys, the "woman" in drag) enter a restaurant where
everything on the menu contains Spam, while some Vikings chant
a wonderful jig about, you guessed it, Spam.

As a tactic in the game, spamming can be occasionally useful.
For example, you know a thief is sneaking up on you to backstab,
and you want to hit him first, so you repeat a "kill <thief>"
command.

This is all well and good, but to prevent people from doing this
exclusively, we added code that begins to cause delays to a character
when they repetitively fail to initiate combat.

It is safe to "spam" 4-5 commands hoping to hit someone, but too
many more than that will cause this delay to begin to kick in.  If
you feel the need to spam, you might want to investigate other options,
such as hunting your victim down instead.
~

0 BLICKED DOOSHED FARMED~
These terms mean killed.  However, they mean more than that.

If a character is blicked, he/she took damage higher than their
maximum hit points.  They were killed instantly.  This term was
originally derived from the "blick" command on Genocide, which
was used to lick the blood of victims, generating a restore.

If a character is dooshed, they died while they were carrying
a blood, which they should probably have drunk.  This term is
derived from the nettrek term for wasting someone that is
carrying armies.

If a character is farmed, their rating is 400 or more points
less than the rating of the character that killed them.  This
is derived from the practice of farming newbies for their blood.
~

0 BREAK~

If you are being strangled, you can 'break' from it.  The break will
lag your opponent.

~
0 GARROTE STRANGLE~

With this skill you can strangle a person, it does some good damage each
combat round according to your opponents constitution.  You need some
kind of wire or 'garrote' to strangle your opponent with.  If you are
being strangled you can use the 'break' command to break free from
your oppnent, the chance of breaking free is dependant on your opponents
strength verse yours.

~

0 SHOOT ARCHER ARCHERY~

With this skill you can use the 'shoot' command.  To be able to shoot
someone you need to be wearing a quiver and wielding a bow.  Also the
person needs to be in your 'line of sight' .. That is they have to be
in a straight line from where you are, with no closed doors, to be able
to shoot them.  Damage is based on the bow you are wielding, you can
use the 'imp identify' spell to see its damage.  But in combat the bows
damage is cut by half.

Archery damage is four times bow damage.  Damroll equipment does
not affect archery.

If you are playing Archer, hunt early.  They have free wheres, and
don't gain anything from equipment hunting.  Prevent dooms by killing.

~

0 RANDOMCLASS RANDOM-CLASS~

When war starts or you join, your class will be randomly picked.
~


0 INVULNERABILITY~


With this spell the victim can take any 1 hit, no matter what kind of
hit..backstab, fireball, slash, and the damage will be 0.. After the
hit the shield will go away.

~
0 WARFLAGS WAR-FLAGS FLAGS~

Current warflags: bloods, continuous, summon, fountains.

There are help on each of these.  At the beginning of each war Army
will pick random flags, some flags are rarer than others though.
Gods may decide to turn off or on flags as they wish.

~

0 FOUNTAIN FOUNTAINS~

Fountains contain liquid, and if you don't already know, any liquid on
pkmud will heal or hurt you.  But in most fountains the liquid will be
to help you, and if the warflag 'fountains' is toggled, all the fountains
should have loaded.

~

0 NOREGEN NO-REGEN WHEEHEE~

If this flag is on, only monks and barbarians may regen during the war.

~

0 BLOOD BLOODS~

If blood war is going on, you should sacrifice player's corpses after you
kill them.. After sacrificing Rip will give you a quart of fresh blood, 
drinking this will heal you to full.
~

0 WRATH~

If the war goes on too long without fighting, the gods will become angry
and fire a doom bolt upon all the mortals, hurting them horribly both
physically and mentally.

~

0 WAR~

See: continuous war, doomsday, join status, status, joinwar, wrath.
~

0 CONTINUOUS 'CONTINUOUS WAR'~

A continuous war simply means it doesnt stop. But, if someone does manage
to kill everyone and be the only person left in war, he is declared the
winner and the mud will reset, then another war may commence.

The join status will go up and down during a continuous war.

Every 40 ticks the mud will reset, all areas and mobs repop.

See also: joinwar, join status, war, doomsday.
~

0 'JOIN STATUS'~

During a war if you type 'who' the join status will be shown. It is
based on the lowest %hp/mana of all the current players in the war.
When you joinwar you will be restored to this %.  In a continuous
war if the join status is low it is wise to wait for someone to die.

See also: joinwar, war, doomsday, continuous war.
~

0 DOOMSDAY~

This is the non-continuous war. When war starts, the doomsday counter is
started. How long until doomsday depends on how many people are
participating in the war.  If doomsday countdown is reached, kaboom,
everyone in war is killed and gets a death.  This is simply a means
to keep wars from lasting indefinately.  Doomsday is not a goal
to be obtained.  Stated simply, doomsday means that everyone loses.
Everyone in war gets a death and nobody gets a win.  

DO NOT INTENTIONALLY CAUSE A WAR TO END BY DOOMSDAY!

If someone kills everyone and is the only person left, he is declared
the winner, and a new war will begin after the mud resets and someone
'starts' the countdown.

See also: joinwar, war, continuous war, start, join status.
~

0 JOINWAR FFA PRIVATE~
Syntax: join/joinwar
Syntax: ffa
Syntax: private <player>

If a war is going on, you can 'join' it via this command. You will be
restored according to the join status.

The ffa command will join a free for all sub-war.  Stats gathered
in this war do not count towards your stats.  Gather equipment with
the oload command, as you cannot kill mobiles.

Private wars can be created between 2 players when they want an informal
war (it does not affect stats) without other people interfering.  Oload,
trans, etc., are disabled in this war type.

See also: war, continuous war, start, join status.
~

0 START~

Type this command to start a war if one is not currently on. A 3-tick
countdown will begin, and then war begins.

There must be at least 2 mortals on to start a war.

See also: war, continuous war, joinwar, join status.
~


