38 ACT~

$n = senders name
$N = victims name

$e = he/she of sender
$E = he/she of victim

$m = him/her of sender
$M = him/her of victim

$s = his/her of sender
$S = his/her of victim

~

0 CALTROPS~

Ninjas can place caltrops via the 'caltrops' command in the room,  they 
are small pointed tac-shaped devices that injure players if they happen 
to walk into a room and land on one.  Ninjas, having been learned in the 
art of caltrops, can avoid them with ease.  The more caltrops in a room 
the more chance of landing on one.

To get some caltrops you must buy them, although you must find a shop 
that sells them yourself.

Syntax: caltrops <number to lay down>

~

0 SMOKE BOMB 'SMOKE BOMB'~

Ninja's create a small magical bomb and hurl it at the ground, covering
the room in smoke.  Only Ninja's can see in the smoke.

Combat and movement cause the smoke to dissipate.
~

0 KI RELEASE 'KI RELEASE'~

This is a spell for monks.  The monk releases all of his inner energy
( ki ) and blasts his victim with it, usually knocking him out of the
room and causing medium damage.

~

0 EGO WHIP 'EGO WHIP'~

This is a pure damage spell for the psionicists.

~

0 TOWER OF ID 'TOWER OF ID'~

This creates a magical buffer damage field around the caster.  For
every x amount of damage, he will take x-10.

~

0 PSIONIC BLAST 'PSIONIC BLAST'~

The caster blasts his psionic energy in all directions, damaging all
in the room, blasting them out of the room, and stunning them.

In addition, victims of this spell may feel a little groggy both
mentally and physicall from this spell.

All effects from this spell have a separate saving throw, and there
is an initial save with a 20% penalty to save against all effects.
~

0 COLOUR COLOR ANSI~
Typing 'colour' will toggle ansi colours.
Color must be on to see any color, including user configurable
options.

Additionally, several colors are user configurable.  The
following options may be set:

gossip, exits, prompt, room_name, say, tell, warmessage

The following colors are valid:

black, blue, cyan, green, magenta, red, white, yellow

Examples:
color gossip red    /* sets gossip to red */
color exits cyan    /* sets exits to cyan */
color tell asdf     /* clears tell color */
~

