-1 STARTING starting~
If you're interested in getting started on PKMud, keep reading, since it
will save you from bugging other players somewhat.  Here are what I feel
are the most asked and important questions:

1) What is this mud all about?
    - This is PKill mud.  The only thing that matters here is killing other
      player characters.  Mobs exist only to get in your way or to hold 
      pieces of equipment you might want.  
2) Ok, so how do I kill other players?  Why can't I lift an arm?              
    - You have to be in war to kill.  (Check the who list, the flag 
      (IN_WAR) shows players who are trying to kill each other).
      To participate, log on before one starts and you are automatically 
      placed in.  You may also join a war once it has started, unless it
      says "too late to join" on the who list message.  If it is possible
      to late join, your hps and mana will be restored according to the 
      percentage shown on the who list message.

See help starting2
~

-1 STARTING2 starting2~
3) What do I do in war?
    - At the start of war, you will be teleported to some random location
      on the mud.  It's a good idea to be wear your equipment and wield
      your weapon.  Now hunt around for other players (to see if one is
      in the same zone as you, use the 'where' command).  It's a good idea
      to also look for equipment to enhance your statistics.  A war ends
      when only one person is left alive.
4) Is there a map?  
    - Yes, type 'help map'.  It's not perfect, but it's a start. 
5) What are the classes and races here?
    - There are no races on PKMud.  To see a list of classes, type 'help
      changeclass' or 'cview', and choose one that suits you.  I would 
      recommend trying them all out at least once.
6) Why is my char deleted every time i come back?
    - This is because in order to save on PKMud, you have to at least kill
      2 people.  Remember even if you do save, it doesn't save any equipment:
      each player starts out with exactly the same weapon and eq each war.
7) Arg! I keep getting my ass kicked.. how can I win?
    - Keep playing.  The more you know about zones, equipment and class
      weaknesses and strengths, the better.  The only advantage one player
      has over another is knowledge of the mud.  

See help starting3
~


-1 starting3 STARTING3 rules~
8) Where can I get some more information (other than the excellent
   helpfiles) about PKmud?
   -Our web pages:
    -Official yet bland - http://www.seas.ucla.edu/-peckham/pkmud/
    -Tips pages - http://www.louisville.edu/-mbdeha01/pkmud.html
                - http://www.geocities.com/SouthBeach/7617	
(The - in the above addresses should be tildes, thats the little squiggly
thing in the top left hand corner of your keyboard.)

RULES OF PKMUD
1)  Remember what you are here for.  The purpose of this mud is to
    kill other players.  If you dont like fighting other players,
    simply put, go away.
2)  Triggers are illegal. <--notice the period at the end of the sentence.
    There are no exceptions.
3)  Intentionally delaying or causing the war to "doomsday" is bad bad bad.
    Dont do it.
4)  Dont spam channels.
5)  Do not multiplay.  Ever.
6)  **Life is not fair**  If you do any of these things prepare to
    get screwed.  Gods have descretion here.  If you are doing something
    you shouldnt be, even if it isnt listed, prepare for the worst.
~	

-1 EXPLORE NEWPLAYER NEWBIE~
One of the most imporant parts to player killing is the hunt.  Because
of this, we have made several modifications to allow players to map
the MUD easier.  The 'GOTO' command is now usable by mortals. You use
it by typing 'goto <mob>', where mob is the name of the monster you want to
find.  The 'TELEPORT' command is useful for exploring random locations.
The 'RECALL' command teleports you to the temple of Ys.

Other commands players should be aware of are WHERE, CHANGECLASS, and
USERS.  (WHERE and CHANGECLASS have help files, USERS is simply a nice
version of WHO that tells you what site people are from, for catching
people playing multiples.)

Also, if you have never played a Diku, you should likely read the help files
for CAST, BASH, etc..  When you use the CHANGECLASS command, you can
assess the classes strengths and weaknesses by using SCORE and PRACTICE.
SCORE will show you that classes max hit points and mana, PRACTICE will
give you a list of skills that class knows. The CVIEW and CVIEW <class> 
command are a new way of determining the advantages and disadvantages 
of different classes.

If you have any questions, ask someone who is on (most people here are nice).

Make sure and read help starting, as it is filled with useful information
and rules for new players.
~

-1 NEWS~
(This file is VERY out of date.  Some entries are hilarious.)

There are no aliases here, please do: help tintin

Food/Drink and Movement were removed, in their normal sense.
Drinking now can heal/harm your health/mana.

Special procedures added to objects.  The One ring and winged boots
are two examples...  Note that spec proc objects do _not_ give you
any message when the proc kicks in...  so pay careful attention to
score.

Please see help news2.
~

-1 NEWS2~

Read "help start".

Where works different now, but costs money, see help where.

Noplay added, see help noplay.

Any lock can now be picked.

Finger command added, victim has to be connected tho...

Changeclass command added.

Please leave a note or email pkmud@pkmud.net if
you see anything that needs fixing.
~



-1 STORY~
PKmud was created in February 1994 to alleviate the tedium of
levelling.

~



